+# SLOW_ENGINE_DESIGN.md — multi-position live path (DESIGN ONLY, no code)
+
+Status: NO Family B hypothesis reached SCREEN_PASS (all 7 KILLED in
+DEV: B1 0.59, B2 −0.33, B3 0.02, B4 turnover-fail, B5 0.64, B6 PBO/
+plateau/turnover-fail, B7 0.15 — see RESEARCH_VERDICTS_B.md). Per E7,
+this file is a DESIGN for a future survivor; no live-path code was
+written, and none may be written until a hypothesis passes the holdout
+screen. The Family A one-position rules are untouched.
+
+## E7.1 Portfolio risk module (reuses existing primitives)
+
+- Gross cap 2× equity, net exposure cap 1× (directional) / 0.2× for
+  dollar-neutral books; per-symbol cap 25% gross (50%/leg only for a
+  re-promoted delta-neutral pair, never above prereg).
+- Vol targeting: trailing-60d portfolio vol scaled to the prereg
+  target; freeze scaling (no up-size) when realized vol exceeds 2×
+  target (vol-spike guard).
+- Per-position isolated liquidation distance: reuse
+  `risk/margin.py:liquidation_ok` per symbol at every rebalance with
+  live `leverageBracket` data; reject the rebalance (hold cash) if any
+  leg violates.
+- Correlated-drawdown cap: halt new entries if trailing-20d average
+  pairwise position correlation × gross exceeds the prereg budget.
+- Daily loss stop 1% / weekly 3% of marked equity (reuse RiskPolicy
+  stop machinery with portfolio-level snapshots); kill switch =
+  existing `enter_safe_mode` + watchdog flatten (already external).
+
+## E7.2 Rebalance scheduler
+
+- Weekly/daily/monthly cadence per prereg; signal computation on
+  closed bars only; no-trade bands exactly as preregistered.
+- Order slicing: limit-first (post-only) up to the no-trade band edge,
+  then TWAP slices over 1h for residuals; partial fills re-sliced next
+  cycle, never chased with market orders beyond the prereg slip model.
+- Reconciliation against venue positions at every rebalance (reuse
+  `seed_from_venue` read path); halt on any break vs expected.
+- Spot legs (B4-class only): supported ONLY if a basis hypothesis
+  passes its screen; spot + perp legs submitted as a pair with a
+  pair-level timeout and a defined unwind order.
+
+## E7.3 Forward-paper harness
+
+- `FORWARD_PAPER` runs the frozen cell on live public data + paper
+  fills with the calibrated pessimistic cost model (never better than
+  the DEV assumption without a fresh verdict).
+- Per-rebalance attribution: predicted vs realized slippage, fees,
+  funding paid/received, latency; drift beyond 1.5× assumed halts.
+- Window: ≥60 days AND ≥30 rebalances (both, per E6.3).
+
+## E7.4 Capital policy
+
+- Sizing: fractional-Kelly (≤ 0.25 Kelly) computed from the bootstrap
+  LOWER bound of expected return, never the point estimate; hard caps
+  (first tranche ≤ min(10% of intended, $500); single-name ≤ 25%).
+- Automatic demotion on: rolling 60d Sharpe < 0, drawdown > 50% of
+  budget, realized costs > 1.5× assumed over 30 rebalances, any
+  unknown order outcome. Promotion manual only (owner + fresh gate).
+
+## E7.5 Gate for Family B (IMPLEMENTED + TESTED, inert without a pass)
+
+`cryptobot gate` accepts `SCREEN_PASS` verdicts only with
+`SEALED-HOLDOUT` provenance (coupling check `screen_requires_holdout`),
+plus autopilot `GATE_READY` (via FORWARD_COMPARE), config-hash match,
+fresh cost model/host-check/drill, measured latency, fresh heartbeat —
+the same human-only `arm` ceremony. Tests:
+`test_autopilot_gate.py::test_gate_family_b_screen_pass_holdout_coupling`.
+Prod refuses without a valid human arm in every path (re-tested).
